meta {
  name: Create Request - duplicate
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/requests
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 500
}

docs {
  ## This asserts current behaviour, not desired behaviour

  Run **Create Request** first, then this. The repository writes with
  `ConditionExpression: attribute_not_exists(PK) AND attribute_not_exists(SK)`, so the
  second write is correctly rejected by DynamoDB -- the row is safe, an APPROVED
  request can't be silently reset to PENDING.

  But `ConditionalCheckFailedException` comes from the AWS SDK and is not a
  `DomainError`, so `GlobalExceptionFilter` falls through to **500 SERVER_ERROR**.
  It should be a 409.

  The fix is a `DuplicateRequestError extends ConflicError` plus a new `ErrorCode`,
  caught in the repository and rethrown. When that lands, change this assertion to
  409 / `DUPLICATE_REQUEST`.
}
